    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00003",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00263:title:sect-00003-title",
        "text": "The Acetoacetic Ester Synthesis"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00016",
          "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00016"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00011",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00011-alt",
              "text": "A reaction in which R-X undergoes acetoacetic ester synthesis to yield methyl ketone. In the product, an R group is attached to C H 2 which in turn is bonded to a carbonyl group attached to a methyl group."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_013.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00017",
          "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00017"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00012",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00012-alt",
              "text": "Ethyl acetoacetate reacts with sodium ethoxide to yield a sodio acetoacetic ester which reacts with R X to generate a monoalkylated acetoacetic ester. The monoalkylated species can be further alkylated using the same approach, the product being a dialkylated acetoacetic ester."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_014.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00018",
          "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00018"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00013",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00013-alt",
              "text": "On heating, an alkylated acetoacetic ester reacts with acid to yield a methyl ketone, C O 2 and ethanol."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_015.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00019",
          "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00019"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00014",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00014-alt",
              "text": "Ethyl 2-oxocyclohexanecarboxylate reacts with sodium ethoxide in first step and benzyl bromide in second step to yield an intermediate which, when heated in acid yields 2-benzylcyclohexanone."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_016.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "example",
          "id": "exam-00002",
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00263:example-title:exam-00002-title",
            "text": "Using Acetoacetic Ester Synthesis to Prepare a Ketone"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00020",
              "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00020"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00021",
              "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00021",
              "title": {
                "segmentId": "m00263:para-title:para-00021-title",
                "text": "Strategy"
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00022",
              "segmentId": "m00263:para:para-00022"
            },
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00023",
              "title": {
                "segmentId": "m00263:para-title:para-00023-title",
                "text": "Solution"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00015",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00015-alt",
              "text": "A structure in which R group is bonded to C H 2 that is bonded to carbonyl bonded to C H 3. The three carbon atoms are from acetoacetic ester."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_017.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00016",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00263:alt:fig-00016-alt",
              "text": "Bromoethane and ethyl acetoacetate react with sodium ethoxide and, following heaing in acid, 2-pentanone is formed."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_22_07_018.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
